        ":question/id": "f5daa79d-c02f-5774-b003-6dd284769848",
        ":question/problem": "Use a calculator to evaluate $\\log_{17}(17)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n$\\log_{17}(17) \\approx$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/requires-calculator": true,
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's calculate $\\log_{17}(17)$ by changing the base $17$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n\\log_a X=\\frac{\\log_b X}{\\log_b a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=17,$ $X=17,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{17}(17) & =\\frac{\\log_{10}(17)}{\\log_{10}(17)} \\\\ & =\\frac{\\log(17)}{\\log(17)} \\\\ & \\approx \\frac{1.230449}{1.230449} \\\\ & \\approx 1.000\\end{aligned}\n$$"
